  <rules>
    <rule name="Melta" id="25dd-f53c-779e-cefb" hidden="false">
      <description>When a weapon with the Melta special rule rolls to penetrate a vehicle&apos;s armour at half range or less, roll an additional D6 and discard the lowest result.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Nova Reactor" id="b202-1002-0002-0003" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of each of its Movement phases, a Riptide can activate its nova reactor. Roll a D6: on a 1, it suffers a wound with no saves allowed; otherwise choose one effect until the start of its next Movement phase. Nova Shield improves its invulnerable save to 3+. Boost lets it make a 4D6&quot; Thrust move. Ripple Fire lets it fire one selected primary weapon twice. Nova-charge uses the corresponding Nova-charge weapon profile.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Sky Ray Missile Defence Gunship" id="b203-1002-0002-0004" hidden="false">
      <description>A Sky Ray is equipped with six seeker missiles and two networked markerlights. Seeker missiles may be fired by friendly markerlight hits as described by the Seeker special rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Supreme Commander" id="b204-2001-0001-0005" hidden="false">
      <description>Friendly Tau Empire units within 12&quot; of Commander Shadowsun may use her Leadership for Morale, Pinning and Regroup tests.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Defender of the Greater Good" id="tau-shadowsun-rule-0001" hidden="false">
      <description>All Stealth Shas&apos;ui and Stealth Shas&apos;vre models in the same unit as Commander Shadowsun have the Sworn Protector special rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Way of the Short Blade" id="b204-2002-0001-0005" hidden="false">
      <description>Commander Farsight and any XV8 Crisis Battlesuit Team he joins have the Preferred Enemy (Orks) special rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Supreme Ethereal" id="b205-2001-0001-0004" hidden="false">
      <description>Friendly Tau Empire units within 12&quot; of Aun&apos;Va may use his Leadership for Morale, Pinning and Regroup tests. He invokes two different elemental powers each turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Supreme Loyalty" id="tau-aunva-rule-0001" hidden="false">
      <description>While Aun&apos;Va is alive, all friendly Tau Empire units on the battlefield re-roll failed Fear, Morale, Pinning and Regroup tests.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Great Invocation" id="tau-aunva-rule-0002" hidden="false">
      <description>When using Invocation of the Elements, Aun&apos;Va can invoke up to two elemental powers each turn rather than one.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Structural Analyser" id="b205-2002-0001-0005" hidden="false">
      <description>When Darkstrider&apos;s unit shoots a non-vehicle enemy unit, that target suffers -1 Toughness against the attacks of Darkstrider&apos;s unit for that Shooting phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Tank Ace" id="b205-2003-0001-0005" hidden="false">
      <description>Longstrike&apos;s Hammerhead has the Tank Hunter special rule and may fire Overwatch with Supporting Fire.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Failure is Not an Option" id="tau-rule-failure-not-option" hidden="false">
      <description>All friendly Tau Empire models within 12&quot; of an Ethereal use his Leadership for Fear, Morale, Pinning and Regroup tests. If the Ethereal is removed as a casualty in a mission that uses Victory Points, the opponent gains one additional Victory Point.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Drone" id="tau-rule-drone" hidden="false">
      <description>A Drone is a model with the Drone unit type. Drones follow the unit-type rules shown in their profile and are ignored where a rule specifically excludes Drones.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Heroic Morale" id="tau-rule-heroic-morale-text" hidden="false">
      <description>A unit with Heroic Morale uses the highest Leadership characteristic in the unit when taking Morale, Pinning and Regroup tests.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Fire Team" id="tau-rule-fire-team-text" hidden="false">
      <description>Whilst a unit with this special rule includes three Vehicles or Monstrous Creatures, all Vehicles and Monstrous Creatures in that unit have +1 Ballistic Skill.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Supporting Fire" id="4f99-5879-4bc6-45d4" hidden="false">
      <description>When an enemy unit declares a charge, all friendly models with this special rule in units within 6&quot; of the charging unit’s target can choose to fire Overwatch as if they were also targets of the charge. Note that a unit can still only fire Overwatch once each phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Invocation of the Elements" id="b201-1001-0004-0001" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of each of your Movement phases, an Ethereal may invoke one elemental power. Until the start of your next turn, friendly non-vehicle Tau Empire units within 12&quot; benefit from that power: Storm of Fire grants an extra shot to pulse weapons at half range; Calm of Tides allows failed Morale and Pinning tests to be re-rolled; Zephyr&apos;s Grace grants the Stubborn special rule; and Sense of Stone grants Feel No Pain (6+).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Volley Fire" id="b201-1002-0005-0001" hidden="false">
      <description>Models in a unit joined by a Cadre Fireblade that did not move in its Movement phase fire an additional shot when shooting pulse rifles or pulse carbines in the Shooting phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Riptide Battlesuit" id="tau-riptide-0026" hidden="false">
      <description>A Riptide battlesuit includes a multi-tracker and blacksun filter.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Riptide Shield Generator" id="tau-riptide-0028" hidden="false">
      <description>The bearer has a 5+ invulnerable save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Stabilising Anchors" id="tau-1008-0002-0007" hidden="false">
      <description>After deploying anchors, the Stormsurge cannot move or make Stomp attacks. From the following Shooting phase it can fire twice; retract anchors at the start of a Movement phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Blademaster" id="tau-rule-blademaster" hidden="false">
      <description>When in a challenge, Aun&apos;Shi must choose a fighting stance each turn before any To Hit rolls are made. Patient Blade lets him re-roll failed saving throws until the end of the current phase. Killing Blade grants Rending until the end of the current phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Sworn Protector" id="tau-rule-sworn-protector" hidden="false">
      <description>An Independent Character in a unit containing at least one model with this special rule automatically passes Look Out, Sir attempts.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Fight on Foot" id="tau-rule-fight-on-foot" hidden="false">
      <description>This model can only join Breacher Teams, Strike Teams or Pathfinder Teams.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Fighting Retreat" id="tau-rule-fighting-retreat" hidden="false">
      <description>Darkstrider and his unit can consolidate D6&quot; in any direction after firing Overwatch, before charge-range rolls are made.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Stealth Field" id="tau-rule-stealth-field" hidden="false">
      <description>All models in a unit with one or more Stealth Drones receive the Stealth special rule, including the Drone. Models that already have Stealth receive Shrouded instead; models that already have both receive no additional benefit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Command-link" id="tau-rule-command-link" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of each friendly Shooting phase, nominate one friendly unit within 12&quot; of this drone. That unit re-rolls To Hit rolls of 1 until the end of the phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="MV52 Shield Generator" id="tau-rule-mv52-shield" hidden="false">
      <description>The bearer has a 3+ invulnerable save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="High Velocity Deployment" id="tau-rule-high-velocity-deployment" hidden="false">
      <description>Interceptor Drones can disembark at any point during the Sun Shark Bomber&apos;s move, even if it has moved at Combat or Cruising Speed. Once disembarked, they count as having moved and cannot fire or embark that turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Interceptor Drone" id="tau-rule-interceptor-drone" hidden="false">
      <description>A Sun Shark Bomber always includes two MV17 Interceptor Drones. They use the Interceptor Drone profile and may deploy using High Velocity Deployment.</description>
    </rule>
  </rules>
